          ("notes" . "Downloads 561.8 MB (gzip.zip, which holds all six EMNIST splits; emnist-balanced, emnist-letters and emnist-digits each download it) and converts the digits split to one row per 28 x 28 grayscale image: the 240,000 training images, then the 40,000 test images, in file order, as torchvision's EMNIST with split=\"digits\" and train=True then train=False. Pixels are pixel1 to pixel784 in row-major order as stored, untransposed as torchvision and TensorFlow Datasets read them: each image is the transpose of the upright character. License NOASSERTION: NIST states no terms and asks that Cohen et al. (2017) be cited; the archive is fetched for use and never redistributed.")
