          ("notes" . "Downloads 2.27 MB (two gzipped text files) and converts them to one row per 16 x 16 USPS digit: the 7,291 training rows, then the 2,007 test rows, in file order. Pixels are pixel1 to pixel256 in row-major order, read as R's read.table reads them, so the 170 -0.0000 values of zip.train.gz stay negative zeros. License NOASSERTION: the book's data page states no terms; the files are fetched for use and never redistributed. The same values are in CRAN ElemStatLearn 2015.6.26.2 (GPL (>= 2)); its zip.test has 68 more negative zeros.")
